  "notes": "SENSE 1 - STEEP:\n- Used for terrain, paths, mountains, cliffs\n- {険|けわ}しい{山|やま} (steep mountain)\n- {険|けわ}しい{道|みち} (steep path)\n\nSENSE 2 - HARSH/STERN:\n- Used for facial expressions, situations\n- {険|けわ}しい{表情|ひょうじょう} (stern expression)\n- {険|けわ}しい{顔|かお} (harsh face)\n- {先行|せんこう}きが{険|けわ}しい (the outlook is grim)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {急|きゅう} (steep, sudden)\n- {厳|きび}しい (strict, severe)\n\nWRITING:\n{険|けん}しい uses the same kanji as {危険|きけん} (danger), reflecting the challenging nature of steep terrain.",
